| **Scheme of ****Learning**** Overview**** - **This concise series of **Digital Learning Workshops** is targeted at academic staff to strategically integrate digital tools, ensuring pedagogical **excellence** and maximizing **impact** on student achievement. The focus is on moving beyond basic use to implementing high-quality digital learning experiences. |
| **SESSION 1**** - ****Teams, Assignments ****&**** Engagement** **Overview:**** **Building a robust, interactive digital ‘home’ that sets high standards for student participation and accountability. **Resources ****&**** Evidence informed pedagogy:** Use **Microsoft Teams** as the central hub for learning. Incorporate **rich media** and collaborative tools to foster active engagement. Design clear submission pathways to reduce ambiguity and improve compliance. **Links to next session:** Explore how digital assessment tools can optimise marking and feedback for improved student outcomes. | **SESSION 2**** - ****Marking, Feedback ****&**** Insights** **Overview:*** *Delivering timely, personalised feedback that addresses gaps and accelerates academic progress. **Resources ****&**** Evidence informed pedagogy:** Employ digital marking tools for efficiency and consistency. Use analytics dashboards to identify trends and inform intervention strategies. Embed feedback loops that set explicit improvement targets **Links to next session:** Discover how **AI can transform learning design** to create challenging, innovative activities. | **SESSION 3**** - ****AI for Innovative Learning Design** **Overview:** Ethically integrating AI to design customised, sophisticated learning experiences that promote critical thinking. **Resources ****&**** Evidence informed pedagogy:** Use AI to **generate diverse, high-quality resources** quickly. Apply AI for **curriculum design innovation**, ensuring alignment with pedagogical principles. Maintain ethical standards and transparency in AI use. **Links to next session:** Learn strategies for **breaking down classroom barriers** and extending learning beyond physical constraints. | **SESSION 4**** - ****Removing Classroom Wall Barriers** **Overview:** Creating seamless, inclusive learning experiences that transcend physical and timetable limitations. **Resources ****&**** Evidence informed pedagogy:** Implement **blended learning strategies** to extend engagement beyond scheduled sessions. Improve accessibility through **digital platforms and assistive technologies**. Foster continuous professional and intellectual development for students. **Links to next session:** Consolidating digital excellence strategies and planning next steps for sustained quality improvement. |

